  "body": "Hello, once I switched to postgres, the size of /var/lib/postgresql is growing day by day.\r\nI'm using my federated synapse server with 3 users and only 1 (myself) is using rooms but just one, not so busy. All the other traffic is private user2user, but just text (no images or media).\r\nIn 2 months my DB is 2.5GB, that's huge for me and it is exausting my VPS free space.\r\n\r\nHere a details for my tables used space: https://hastebin.com/eyafomoxox.cs\r\n\r\n790MB of public.state_groups_state only.\r\n\r\nHow can I free up space? I tried vacuuming that table but I gain 3 MB only.\r\nCan you help me? I found  various scripts to purge old rooms and so on, but I'm searching something to simply  purging anything older than 2 months, without having to specify rooms ID or something.\r\nI don't want to waste all that space...\r\n\r\nThanks for your help!",
